    "explanation": "Rider — the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on 10 Aug 2026 is refunded to you in full. Driver — no compensation is payable on this trip.\n\nThe booking was an advance (scheduled) trip. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02738) shows it was accepted at 17:10:08 and scheduled for pickup at 17:55:08, and the rider cancelled at 17:35:08 — 1,200 seconds (20 minutes) before the scheduled time. POL-NS-10(b) provides that, for a scheduled trip, a cancellation made more than the advance grace of 900 seconds (15 minutes) before the scheduled time is not chargeable, and 1,200 seconds is more than 900 seconds. POL-NS-10(c) then requires the SGD 4.50 fee to be refunded in full with no driver compensation. The refunded amount is the cancellation-fee line of the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02738: cancellation_fee SGD 4.50, total_charged SGD 4.50), which matches platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50. The fare lines reconcile, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect — but a correctly stated fee can still be non-chargeable, and this one is.\n\nDriver's arguments. Your claim that the rider's own cancellation is chargeable under POL-NS-10(f) fails because limb (f) reaches only cancellations that fall outside both protective windows, limbs (a) and (b); this cancellation falls inside limb (b)'s protection. Your reading of limb (b) — that a cancellation 1,200 seconds before the scheduled time is 'well inside' a 900-second window — reverses the test: 1,200 is more than 900, so the fee is not chargeable, and the rider's own statement that she cancelled 'twenty minutes before' is the fact that defeats the charge. You are right that limb (a) does not protect the rider (the cancellation was 1,500 seconds after acceptance, past the 180-second match grace) and that the fee reconciles, but neither point helps once limb (b) applies. Your no-show case under POL-NS-01 is not made out: there is no 'arrived' event, arrived_at is null, the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02738) keeps the driver's fixes roughly 14 km or more from the pick-up pin, and the qualifying in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 180-second free-wait minimum — a point both sides accept. Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full and POL-NS-10(g) does not apply (the rider cancelled before any arrival), POL-NS-07 cannot pay you: the anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations in 30 days against 90 completed trips, ratio 0.022), but no compensation arises in any event, and the driver-side loss argument does not create one where the clause's gateway is unmet.\n\nRider's other points. POL-NS-02 (the driver never entered the 50 m arrival radius), POL-NS-06 (zero dwell against the 180-second minimum) and POL-NS-04 (the chat log is empty, so no unanswered locating message) all point the same way or are moot; none of them changes the outcome, which POL-NS-10(b) decides. The rider's passing reference to POL-NS-10(f)'s ETA exception does not need to be reached, for the same reason limb (f) does not apply at all.\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is 0.92, above the 0.70 floor. The deciding facts — the scheduled time, the acceptance time, the cancellation time and the fee — are carried by EV-TRIP-02738 and EV-FARE-02738, each at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02738-01, weight 0.0) is not relied on, because POL-NS-10(b) does not require it, so it neither caps confidence nor triggers escalation; the GPS trace is complete (157 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, rider track present) and is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). Neither profile shows counterparty disputes, no abuse threshold is met, and the two admissible instruments do not contradict each other. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes automatically."
  },
