    "explanation": "To both parties. This was an advance (scheduled) booking: the trip was accepted at 17:10:08 for a 17:55:08 pickup, and the rider cancelled at 17:35:08 under reason code RIDER_CANCELLED. The cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 was charged and is now refunded in full. Decision: FULL_REFUND of SGD 4.50, with no driver compensation. Why the fee does not stand: POL-NS-10(b) provides that on a scheduled trip a cancellation made MORE than the advance grace of 900 seconds (15 minutes) before the scheduled pickup is not chargeable. The rider cancelled 1200 seconds (20 minutes) before 17:55:08, which is more than the 900-second grace, so the cancellation falls inside the free-cancellation window, and POL-NS-10(c) requires the whole fee back with no driver compensation. The trip was accepted 2700 seconds before the scheduled time, well outside the 900-second window, so the shorter 180-second match grace in limb (a) does not apply either. The driver's argument that 1200 seconds is 'inside' the 900-second window is rejected: 1200 exceeds 900, so the cancellation was early enough to be free, and his POL-NS-10(f) argument does not reach these facts, because (f) makes a rider's own cancellation chargeable only once the grace in (a) or (b) has run out - that is, within 15 minutes of the scheduled pickup - which this cancellation was not. The same result follows independently on the driver's side of the case. There is no 'arrived' event and arrived_at is null; the GPS trace places the driver between about 14 km and 40 km from the pickup pin throughout, with zero in-geofence fixes and zero qualifying dwell against the 180-second free waiting period. POL-NS-01 therefore fails at limbs (a), (b) and (c) - as the driver's own brief concedes - and POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 each require the cancellation fee to be refunded in full. POL-NS-01 limb (d) would fail too, the trip having been cancelled by the rider rather than terminated by the driver for a no-show. Driver compensation: none. POL-NS-10(c), POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 each bar it, and POL-NS-07's payout route is not reached because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full and POL-NS-10(g) does not apply (the driver never arrived). The anti-farming check does not trip in any event (no_show_terminations_30d 2, below 4; 2/90 = 0.022, below 0.08), so no escalation packet is produced; the lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags is context only and was not used. Evidence and weight: the deciding facts - the cancellation timestamps and reason code, and the driver's position - are carried by EV-TRIP-02738 and EV-GPS-02738, each fully admissible at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence 0.92 sits below it. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02738-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries nothing; no part of this refund rests on it, and the rider's POL-NS-06 shortfall argument is reached on the GPS alone. The fare line of SGD 4.50 reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. On the remaining points: the rider was at the pin (3.93 m) at cancellation and the chat log is empty, so this is neither a POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance case nor a POL-NS-04 coordination-failure case - the rider simply does not need either clause, because the fee fails on the cancellation timing and on the driver's non-arrival. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the trip record and GPS agree rather than contradict, there are no same-party disputes in the trailing 90 days, the anti-farming check is clear, and the deciding facts are carried by weight-1.0 artifacts. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically; this is a provisional ruling and either party may appeal it once within 30 days.",
